\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Impulse responses of the state unemployment rate (left) and vacancy rate (right) to a one-standard-deviation increase in the residualised $\delta $ Bartik instrument ($\hat  {\sigma }_{\tilde  {B}^\delta }=14.0$ pp, 2001Q1--2019Q4). Both outcomes are estimated from panel local projections with state and time fixed effects; standard errors are clustered at the state level ($n=50$). Shaded band: 90\% confidence interval; dashed lines: 95\% confidence interval. The instrument is BED establishment deaths (equation~\MT_extended_eqref:n  {eq:bartik_delta}), residualized on aggregate productivity growth and lagged industry value-added growth (equation~\MT_extended_eqref:n  {eq:resid_v2}). Outcome window capped at 2019Q4 to exclude COVID.}}{36}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\MT@newlabel{eq:bartik_delta}
